sc-2-p5 = prose (cons "Here `mn-call1` uses the source definition `f` as its fallback if the modeled machine run does not return an ordinary result. Consequently `Correct1` by itself does **not** assert that all machine runs terminate, that all bytes have an ordinary return, or that the target semantics is fully proved correct for arbitrary programs. Its definition is precise; the separate correctness argument must address the machine cases that matter. The relation between specialized terms and their original definitions is checked at the term level. A theorem connecting emitted bytes to the instruction semantics additionally requires proofs of the encoder templates under the chosen machine model. These are distinct composable proof obligations over the same interpreted computation." nil)
